= The February Revolution

Eight days of strikes, bread riots and mutinies have overthrown the Romanov dynasty. Nicholas II abdicated on 15 March. In the Tauride Palace two authorities have appeared: a Provisional Government of liberals under Prince Lvov, and the Petrograd Soviet of Workers' and Soldiers' Deputies, in which the Mensheviks and the SRs hold the majority, with Chkheidze in the chair.

The Soviet commands the garrison, the railways and the telegraph. The government commands the ministries. Neither can do without the other. The Kadet leader Milyukov is Foreign Minister, and the only socialist in the cabinet is the SR lawyer Kerensky, who joined without asking the Soviet.

What should the party do?

- @control: Lead the Soviet as a control body, and stay out of the government.
- @enter: Take ministries in the first cabinet.
- @soviet_gov: Demand a Soviet government now.
- @sr_outside: Back Kerensky as the Soviet's man, and keep the party out of the government.
- @sr_enter: Take ministries for the party.
- @sr_soviet_gov: Demand a Soviet government now.

@control
view-if: player_party = 'menshevik'
on-arrival: {!
Q.in_coalition = 0;
RO.add(Q, {rel_kad: 3, rel_ally: 3});
RO.fac(Q, 'defencist', 2, 0);
!}

Our reading of the revolution is that it is a bourgeois one, and that the bourgeoisie must govern. The Soviet will watch, advise and, when necessary, restrain it. It is a role that is both powerful and irresponsible.

@enter
view-if: player_party = 'menshevik'
on-arrival: {!
Q.in_coalition = 1;
Q.gov_kadets = 1;
RO.add(Q, {rel_kad: 6, bolshevik: 2});
RO.fac(Q, 'defencist', 4, 0);
RO.fac(Q, 'intl', -2, 10);
Q.resources += 1;
!}

Chkheidze was offered the Ministry of Labour. We have chosen to share responsibility with the liberals from the first day. [+ Ilbl +] object that we will share the blame as well.

@soviet_gov
view-if: player_party = 'menshevik'
choose-if: rel_ally >= 60
unavailable-subtitle: The SRs will not agree to this.
on-arrival: {!
Q.in_coalition = 1;
Q.gov_kadets = 0;
Q.homogeneous_gov = 1;
RO.add(Q, {rel_kad: -20, right_threat: 12, ruble: -5, soviet_democracy: 3, army_discipline: 2});
RO.boost(Q, {workers: 3, soldiers: 3, middle: -5});
RO.fac(Q, 'intl', 4, -5);
RO.fac(Q, 'defencist', -4, 8);
RO.fac(Q, 'rightdef', 0, 10);
!}

The Menshevik and SR leaders have formed a government of the Soviet parties. The officers are alarmed and the Allies have withheld recognition. The Marxist doctrine that the revolution is a bourgeois one has been set aside, and nobody can say what will replace it.

@sr_outside
view-if: player_party = 'sr'
on-arrival: {!
Q.in_coalition = 0;
RO.add(Q, {rel_kad: 3, rel_ally: 3});
RO.fac(Q, 'defencist', 2, 0);
RO.fac(Q, 'rightdef', 0, 4);
!}

Kerensky has joined the cabinet as Minister of Justice, as an individual and without asking his party. The Party Council has said that the party will not follow him in, and has made clear that it will not turn him out, either. He is the Soviet's man in the government, and the Soviet's chosen hostage.

@sr_enter
view-if: player_party = 'sr'
on-arrival: {!
Q.in_coalition = 1;
Q.gov_kadets = 1;
RO.add(Q, {rel_kad: 6, bolshevik: 2});
RO.fac(Q, 'defencist', 2, 0);
RO.fac(Q, 'rightdef', 3, -3);
RO.fac(Q, 'intl', -2, 10);
Q.resources += 1;
!}

The party has taken ministries, beside Kerensky and the liberals. The Right SRs call it a historic duty. The Left SRs say that the party has sold the revolution before it has begun.

@sr_soviet_gov
view-if: player_party = 'sr'
choose-if: rel_ally >= 60
unavailable-subtitle: The Mensheviks will not agree to this.
on-arrival: {!
Q.in_coalition = 1;
Q.gov_kadets = 0;
Q.homogeneous_gov = 1;
RO.add(Q, {rel_kad: -20, right_threat: 12, ruble: -5, soviet_democracy: 3, army_discipline: 2});
RO.boost(Q, {workers: 3, soldiers: 3, middle: -5});
RO.fac(Q, 'intl', 4, -5);
RO.fac(Q, 'defencist', 2, 3);
RO.fac(Q, 'rightdef', -3, 10);
!}

The SR and Menshevik leaders have formed a government of the Soviet parties. The officers are alarmed and the Allies have withheld recognition. The party that has the votes of the peasants has taken the responsibility of power in the first week of the revolution.
